cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build Argus for published work, please cite it as below and note the release tag corresponding to the parts you printed."
title: "Argus: a multi-height 360 degree camera rig for systematic interior reality capture"
abstract: >-
  Argus is an open-hardware rig that mounts three consumer 360 degree cameras
  at fixed, repeatable elevations so that a single walk through a building
  produces the vertical baseline and occlusion coverage that structure-from-
  motion reconstruction requires. Built from 3D printed parts and off-the-shelf
  hardware. Designed to be planned and processed with the companion Hera
  software.
# CFF only supports "software" and "dataset" as types; there is no hardware
# type. "software" is the conventional choice for open-hardware projects.
